<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ CHEs decrease deficit in June yr to NZ$164 mln.</title>
<headline>NZ CHEs decrease deficit in June yr to NZ$164 mln.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>New Zealand Crown Health Enterprises (CHEs) in total recorded an operating deficit of NZ$164.2 million for the year to June 30, Statistics New Zealand said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>This was a 17.5 percent decrease from the June 1995 year deficit of $199.1 million.</p>
<p>Twenty-one CHEs recorded deficits at the end of June 1996.</p>
<p>The debt position of the CHEs as at June 30 was $1.154 billion, up $93.4 million compared to the position one year ago, when total debt was $1.060 billion, SNZ said.</p>
<p>-- Wellington Newsroom (64 4) 4734746</p>
